# CS-101: Front-End Canvas Telemetry & Syntax Assignment

A practical laboratory environment exploring standard HTML5 Canvas layouts, semantic CSS structures, and modular tracking variables. Designed for student syntax testing and browser interface rendering.

## 🛠️ Implementation Requirements
* Ensure all elements render inside semantic block components.
* Maintain lightweight frame timing cycles.
* Test cross-browser compatibility for viewport scaling parameters.

## 📈 Current Project Milestones
- [x] Create core structure file (`index.html`)
- [x] Configure coordinate tracking vectors
- [x] Establish responsive stylesheet boilerplates
- [ ] Implement data output telemetry nodes

## 📑 Compilation Notes
This environment relies strictly on pure client-side web technology rules. No external server dependencies, backend frameworks, or localized database storage allocations are required for standard compilation tasks.
